    <head>
        <drug>
            <atcs>
                <atc>J01XA01</atc>
            </atcs>
            <activeSubstances>
                <activeSubstance>vancomycin</activeSubstance>
            </activeSubstances>
            <drugName>
                <name lang='en'>Vancomycin</name>
                <name lang='fr'>Vancomycine</name>
            </drugName>
            <drugDescription>
                <desc lang='en'>Vancomycin is a glycopeptide antibiotic medication used to treat certain bacterial infections. It is administered intravenously (injection into a vein) to treat complicated skin infections, bloodstream infections, endocarditis, bone and joint infections, and meningitis caused by methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus.</desc>
                <desc lang='fr'>La vancomycine est un antibiotique glycopeptidique utilisé pour traiter certaines infections bactériennes. Elle est administrée par voie intraveineuse (injection dans une veine) pour traiter les infections cutanées compliquées, les infections sanguines, l’endocardite, les infections osseuses et articulaires, ainsi que la méningite causées par Staphylococcus aureus résistant à la méthicilline.</desc>
            </drugDescription>
            <tdmStrategy>
                <text lang='en'>The efficacy of vancomycin is best predicted by the AUC of circulating concentrations over MIC of the target bacteria. The MIC of most sensitive bacterias is below 1 mg/L, a value usually considered when the actual MIC of the bacterial strain infecting the patient has not been determined. The most usual recommendation regarding AUC/MIC value in the literature is to keep it above 400 h over a one-day interval. This can equivalently be expressed in terms of average concentration with a corresponding minimum target of 17 times the MIC, or 17 mg/L assuming a MIC of 1 mg/L. We use practically a target of 500 h, with an acceptance interval of 400 to 700 h. Accordingly, the concentration target that we recommend for a continuous infusion is 15-25 mg/L.
                                                                                                Another traditional method of dosage optimization often proposed for vancomycin given as intermittent infusion is to target a trough concentration of 10-15 mg/L. Yet a higher target of 15-20 mg/L is recommended for MRSA and other severe infections with Enterococcus of high resistance potential.</text>
                <text lang='fr'>L’efficacité de la vancomycine est mieux prédite par le rapport AUC des concentrations circulantes sur la CMI de la bactérie cible. La CMI de la plupart des bactéries sensibles est inférieure à 1 mg/L, une valeur généralement retenue lorsque la CMI réelle de la souche bactérienne infectant le patient n’a pas été déterminée. La recommandation la plus courante concernant le rapport AUC/CMI dans la littérature est de le maintenir au-dessus de 400 h sur un intervalle d’un jour. Cela peut être exprimé de manière équivalente en termes de concentration moyenne avec un objectif minimum correspondant de 17 fois la CMI, soit 17 mg/L en supposant une CMI de 1 mg/L. Nous utilisons pratiquement un objectif de 500 h, avec un intervalle d’acceptation de 400 à 700 h. En conséquence, la concentration cible que nous recommandons pour une perfusion continue est de 15 à 25 mg/L.</text>
            </tdmStrategy>
        </drug>
        <study>
            <studyName>
                <name lang='en'>Optimisation of vancomycin exposure in neonates based on the best level of evidence</name>
            </studyName>
            <studyAuthors>Dao K, Guidi M, André P, Giannoni E, Basterrechea S, Zhao W, Fuchs A, Pfister M, Buclin T, Csajka C.</studyAuthors>
            <description>
                <desc lang='en'>A total 405 neonates provided 1831 vancomycin concentrations measured during routine TDM. A one-compartment model with linear elimination incorporating covariates such as age, kidney function and body weight was developed with NONMEM. The final model was applied to simulate in our population vancomycin exposure resulting from 20 dosing guidelines identified in the literature.</desc>
            </description>
            <references>
                <reference type='bibtex'>
                    <![CDATA[@article{Dao2020,
                                                              title = {Optimisation of vancomycin exposure in neonates based on the best level of evidence},
                                                              journal = {Pharmacological Research},
                                                              volume = {154},
                                                              pages = {104278},
                                                              year = {2020},
                                                              doi = {10.1016/j.phrs.2019.104278},
                                                              url = {https://doi.org/10.1016/j.phrs.2019.104278},
                                                              author = {Kim Dao and Monia Guidi and Pascal André and Eric Giannoni and Sébastien Basterrechea and Wei Zhao and Aline Fuchs and Marc Pfister and Thierry Buclin and Chantal Csajka},
                                                              keywords = {Vancomycin, Neonates, Pharmacokinetics, Dosing Regimens, Therapeutic Drug Monitoring, AUC/MIC, Trough Concentration},
                                                              abstract = {There is no consensus regarding optimal dosing of vancomycin in term or preterm neonates. Various available dosing recommendations are based on age, kidney function and/or body weight to define a starting dose. Our objectives were (i) to develop a comprehensive population PK model of vancomycin in a large cohort of neonates and (ii) to evaluate and compare the performances of current dosing approaches with respect to target attainment, using simulations based on our model. This will serve the purpose to recommend the best dosing approaches among existing regimens in the early and later phases after treatment initiation as a complementary approach to therapeutic drug monitoring (TDM). A total 405 neonates provided 1831 vancomycin concentrations measured during routine TDM. A one-compartment model with linear elimination incorporating covariates such as age, kidney function and body weight was developed (NONMEM®). The final model was applied to simulate in our population vancomycin exposure resulting from 20 dosing guidelines identified in the literature. Proportions of patients within and above target exposure were used as a performance measure. Target attainment meant area under the curve/minimal inhibitory concentration (AUC_{24}/MIC) ratio of 400-700 h and trough concentration of 10-20 mg/L, both on days 1 and 7. Most current vancomycin dosing regimens fail to ensure target attainment in a majority of neonates. Insufficiently dosed regimens should be avoided, especially in centers with widespread coagulase negative Staphylococci. Adding a loading dose to simple regimens is best recommended to increase the proportion of early target attainment. Complex regimens seem to marginally improve exposure. Optimisation of efficacy while minimizing toxicity of vancomycin in neonates is needed. The application of a simple dosing regimens like NNF7 or the Neofax Hi-Dose regimens, with a 25 mg/kg loading dose for severe infections, or the SmPC regimen should be recommended to ensure the highest proportion of target attainment after 24 h. TDM should then be carried out, to account for residual unexplained variability in vancomycin elimination.}
                                                            }]]>
                </reference>
                <reference type='doi'>
                    <![CDATA[https://doi.org/10.1016/j.phrs.2019.104278]]>
                </reference>
            </references>
        </study>
        <comments/>
    </head>
    <drugModel>
        <drugId>vancomycin</drugId>
        <drugModelId>ch.tucuxi.vancomycin.dao2019</drugModelId>
        <domain>
            <description>
                <desc lang='en'>Neonate patients treated with intermittent IV vancomycin for bacterial infections, aged 0-0.5 years, weight 0-10 kg.</desc>
                <desc lang='fr'>Nourrissons traités par vancomycine IV intermittente pour des infections bactériennes, âgés de 0 à 0,5 an, pesant de 0 à 10 kg.</desc>
            </description>
            <constraints>
                <constraint>
                    <constraintType>hard</constraintType>
                    <errorMessage>
                        <text lang='en'>The study includes a population aged from 0 to 0.5 years.</text>
                        <text lang='fr'>L&apos;étude est basée sur une population agée de 0 à 0.5 an.</text>
                    </errorMessage>
                    <requiredCovariates>
                        <covariateId>postnatalage</covariateId>
                    </requiredCovariates>
                    <checkOperation>
                        <softFormula>
                            <inputs>
                                <input>
                                    <id>postnatalage</id>
                                    <type>double</type>
                                </input>
                            </inputs>
                            <code>
                                <![CDATA[
                                return ((postnatalage > 0) && (postnatalage <= 168));
                                ]]>
                            </code>
                        </softFormula>
                        <comments/>
                    </checkOperation>
                    <comments/>
                </constraint>
                <constraint>
                    <constraintType>hard</constraintType>
                    <errorMessage>
                        <text lang='en'>The study includes a population weighing between 0 and 10 kg.</text>
                        <text lang='fr'>L&apos;étude est basée sur une population pesant entre 0 et 10 kg.</text>
                    </errorMessage>
                    <requiredCovariates>
                        <covariateId>bodyweight</covariateId>
                    </requiredCovariates>
                    <checkOperation>
                        <softFormula>
                            <inputs>
                                <input>
                                    <id>bodyweight</id>
                                    <type>double</type>
                                </input>
                            </inputs>
                            <code>
                                <![CDATA[
                                return ((bodyweight > 0) && (bodyweight <= 10));
                                ]]>
                            </code>
                        </softFormula>
                        <comments/>
                    </checkOperation>
                    <comments/>
                </constraint>
            </constraints>
        </domain>
        <covariates>
            <covariate>
                <covariateId>gestationalage</covariateId>
                <covariateName>
                    <name lang='en'>gestational age</name>
                    <name lang='fr'>âge gestationnel</name>
                </covariateName>
                <description>
                    <desc lang='en'>Patient&apos;s gestational age in weeks.</desc>
                    <desc lang='fr'>Âge gestationnel du patient en semaines.</desc>
                </description>
                <unit>week</unit>
                <covariateType>standard</covariateType>
                <dataType>double</dataType>
                <interpolationType>linear</interpolationType>
                <refreshPeriod>
                    <unit>w</unit>
                    <value>1</value>
                </refreshPeriod>
                <covariateValue>
                    <standardValue>40</standardValue>
                </covariateValue>
                <validation>
                    <errorMessage>
                        <text lang='en'>Gestational age must be between 20 and 45 weeks.</text>
                        <text lang='fr'>L&apos;âge gestationnel doit être compris entre 20 et 45 semaines.</text>
                    </errorMessage>
                    <operation>
                        <softFormula>
                            <inputs>
                                <input>
                                    <id>gestationalage</id>
                                    <type>double</type>
                                </input>
                            </inputs>
                            <code>
                                <![CDATA[
                                return ((gestationalage > 20) && (gestationalage < 45));
                                ]]>
                            </code>
                        </softFormula>
                        <comments/>
                    </operation>
                    <comments/>
                </validation>
                <comments/>
            </covariate>
            <covariate>
                <covariateId>postnatalage</covariateId>
                <covariateName>
                    <name lang='en'>postnatal age</name>
                    <name lang='fr'>âge post-natal</name>
                </covariateName>
                <description>
                    <desc lang='en'>Patient&apos;s postnatal age in weeks.</desc>
                    <desc lang='fr'>Âge post-natal du patient en semaines.</desc>
                </description>
                <unit>week</unit>
                <covariateType>ageInWeeks</covariateType>
                <dataType>double</dataType>
                <interpolationType>linear</interpolationType>
                <refreshPeriod>
                    <unit>w</unit>
                    <value>1</value>
                </refreshPeriod>
                <covariateValue>
                    <standardValue>1</standardValue>
                </covariateValue>
                <validation>
                    <errorMessage>
                        <text lang='en'>Postnatal age must be positive.</text>
                        <text lang='fr'>L&apos;âge post-natal doit être positif.</text>
                    </errorMessage>
                    <operation>
                        <softFormula>
                            <inputs>
                                <input>
                                    <id>postnatalage</id>
                                    <type>double</type>
                                </input>
                            </inputs>
                            <code>
                                <![CDATA[
                                return (postnatalage > 0);
                                ]]>
                            </code>
                        </softFormula>
                        <comments/>
                    </operation>
                    <comments/>
                </validation>
                <comments/>
            </covariate>
            <covariate>
                <covariateId>bodyweight</covariateId>
                <covariateName>
                    <name lang='en'>body weight</name>
                    <name lang='fr'>poids</name>
                </covariateName>
                <description>
                    <desc lang='en'>Patient&apos;s body weight in kg.</desc>
                    <desc lang='fr'>Poids du patient en kg.</desc>
                </description>
                <unit>kg</unit>
                <covariateType>standard</covariateType>
                <dataType>double</dataType>
                <interpolationType>linear</interpolationType>
                <refreshPeriod>
                    <unit>d</unit>
                    <value>1</value>
                </refreshPeriod>
                <covariateValue>
                    <standardValue>3</standardValue>
                </covariateValue>
                <validation>
                    <errorMessage>
                        <text lang='en'>Body weight must be positive.</text>
                        <text lang='fr'>Le poids doit être positif.</text>
                    </errorMessage>
                    <operation>
                        <softFormula>
                            <inputs>
                                <input>
                                    <id>bodyweight</id>
                                    <type>double</type>
                                </input>
                            </inputs>
                            <code>
                                <![CDATA[
                                return (bodyweight >= 0);
                                ]]>
                            </code>
                        </softFormula>
                        <comments/>
                    </operation>
                    <comments/>
                </validation>
                <comments/>
            </covariate>
            <covariate>
                <covariateId>creatinine</covariateId>
                <covariateName>
                    <name lang='en'>serum creatinine concentration</name>
                    <name lang='fr'>concentration de sérum créatinine</name>
                </covariateName>
                <description>
                    <desc lang='en'>Patient&apos;s serum creatinine concentration in umol/L.</desc>
                    <desc lang='fr'>Concentration de sérum créatinine du patient en umol/L.</desc>
                </description>
                <unit>umol/l</unit>
                <covariateType>standard</covariateType>
                <dataType>double</dataType>
                <interpolationType>linear</interpolationType>
                <refreshPeriod>
                    <unit>d</unit>
                    <value>1</value>
                </refreshPeriod>
                <covariateValue>
                    <standardValue>35</standardValue>
                </covariateValue>
                <validation>
                    <errorMessage>
                        <text lang='en'>Serum creatinine concentration must be positive.</text>
                        <text lang='fr'>La concentration de sérum créatinine doit être positif.</text>
                    </errorMessage>
                    <operation>
                        <softFormula>
                            <inputs>
                                <input>
                                    <id>creatinine</id>
                                    <type>double</type>
                                </input>
                            </inputs>
                            <code>
                                <![CDATA[
                                return (creatinine > 0);
                                ]]>
                            </code>
                        </softFormula>
                        <comments/>
                    </operation>
                    <comments/>
                </validation>
                <comments/>
            </covariate>
        </covariates>
        <activeMoieties>
            <activeMoiety>
                <activeMoietyId>vancomycin</activeMoietyId>
                <activeMoietyName>
                    <name lang='en'>vancomycin</name>
                </activeMoietyName>
                <unit>mg/l</unit>
                <analyteIdList>
                    <analyteId>vancomycin</analyteId>
                </analyteIdList>
                <analytesToMoietyFormula>
                    <hardFormula>direct</hardFormula>
                    <comments/>
                </analytesToMoietyFormula>
                <targets>
                    <target>
                        <targetType>auc24DividedByMic</targetType>
                        <targetValues>
                            <unit>h</unit>
                            <min>
                                <standardValue>400</standardValue>
                            </min>
                            <max>
                                <standardValue>700</standardValue>
                            </max>
                            <best>
                                <standardValue>540</standardValue>
                            </best>
                            <toxicityAlarm>
                                <standardValue>1000</standardValue>
                            </toxicityAlarm>
                            <inefficacyAlarm>
                                <standardValue>100</standardValue>
                            </inefficacyAlarm>
                            <mic>
                                <unit>mg/l</unit>
                                <micValue>
                                    <standardValue>1</standardValue>
                                </micValue>
                            </mic>
                        </targetValues>
                        <comments/>
                    </target>
                </targets>
            </activeMoiety>
        </activeMoieties>
        <analyteGroups>
            <analyteGroup>
                <groupId>vancomycin</groupId>
                <pkModelId>linear.1comp.macro</pkModelId>
                <analytes>
                    <analyte>
                        <analyteId>vancomycin</analyteId>
                        <unit>mg/l</unit>
                        <molarMass>
                            <value>1449.3</value>
                            <unit>g/mol</unit>
                        </molarMass>
                        <description/>
                        <errorModel>
                            <errorModelType>mixed</errorModelType>
                            <sigmas>
                                <sigma>
                                    <standardValue>1.98</standardValue>
                                </sigma>
                                <sigma>
                                    <standardValue>0.236</standardValue>
                                </sigma>
                            </sigmas>
                            <comments/>
                        </errorModel>
                        <comments/>
                    </analyte>
                </analytes>
                <dispositionParameters>
                    <parameters>
                        <parameter>
                            <parameterId>CL</parameterId>
                            <unit>l/h</unit>
                            <parameterValue>
                                <standardValue>0.273</standardValue>
                                <aprioriComputation>
                                    <softFormula>
                                        <inputs>
                                            <input>
                                                <id>postnatalage</id>
                                                <type>double</type>
                                            </input>
                                            <input>
                                                <id>gestationalage</id>
                                                <type>double</type>
                                            </input>
                                            <input>
                                                <id>bodyweight</id>
                                                <type>double</type>
                                            </input>
                                            <input>
                                                <id>creatinine</id>
                                                <type>double</type>
                                            </input>
                                        </inputs>
                                        <code>
                                            <![CDATA[
                                            median_bodyweight = 1;
                                            median_scr = 54;
                                            Hill = 3.54;
                                            T50 = 46.4;
                                            PMA = gestationalage + postnatalage;
                                            theta_CL = 0.273;
                                            theta_bodyweight = 0.438;
                                            theta_scr = 0.473;
                                            
                                            cl1 = theta_CL * Math.pow((bodyweight/median_bodyweight),theta_bodyweight);
                                            cl2 = cl1 * Math.pow((median_scr/creatinine),theta_scr);
                                            cl3 = cl2 * (Math.pow(PMA,Hill) / (Math.pow(PMA,Hill) + Math.pow(T50,Hill)));
                                            
                                            if (cl3 < 0) {
                                              cl3 = 0.001;
                                            }
                                            
                                            return cl3;
                                            ]]>
                                        </code>
                                    </softFormula>
                                    <comments/>
                                </aprioriComputation>
                            </parameterValue>
                            <bsv>
                                <bsvType>exponential</bsvType>
                                <stdDevs>
                                    <stdDev>0.226</stdDev>
                                </stdDevs>
                            </bsv>
                            <validation>
                                <errorMessage>
                                    <text lang='en'>Error in PK parameter (CL).</text>
                                </errorMessage>
                                <operation>
                                    <softFormula>
                                        <inputs>
                                            <input>
                                                <id>CL</id>
                                                <type>double</type>
                                            </input>
                                        </inputs>
                                        <code>
                                            <![CDATA[
                                            return CL > 0.0;
                                            ]]>
                                        </code>
                                    </softFormula>
                                    <comments/>
                                </operation>
                                <comments/>
                            </validation>
                            <comments/>
                        </parameter>
                        <parameter>
                            <parameterId>V</parameterId>
                            <unit>l</unit>
                            <parameterValue>
                                <standardValue>0.628</standardValue>
                                <aprioriComputation>
                                    <softFormula>
                                        <inputs>
                                            <input>
                                                <id>bodyweight</id>
                                                <type>double</type>
                                            </input>
                                        </inputs>
                                        <code>
                                            <![CDATA[
                                            median_BW = 1;
                                                                                                        theta_V = 0.628;
                                                                                                        v1 = theta_V * bodyweight/median_BW;
                                                                                                        if (v1 < 0) {
                                                                                                          v1 = 0.001;
                                                                                                        }
                                                                                                        return v1;
                                            ]]>
                                        </code>
                                    </softFormula>
                                    <comments/>
                                </aprioriComputation>
                            </parameterValue>
                            <bsv>
                                <bsvType>none</bsvType>
                                <stdDevs />
                            </bsv>
                            <validation>
                                <errorMessage>
                                    <text lang='en'>Error in PK parameter (V).</text>
                                </errorMessage>
                                <operation>
                                    <softFormula>
                                        <inputs>
                                            <input>
                                                <id>V</id>
                                                <type>double</type>
                                            </input>
                                        </inputs>
                                        <code>
                                            <![CDATA[
                                            return V > 0.0;
                                            ]]>
                                        </code>
                                    </softFormula>
                                    <comments/>
                                </operation>
                                <comments/>
                            </validation>
                            <comments/>
                        </parameter>
                    </parameters>
                    <correlations />
                </dispositionParameters>
            </analyteGroup>
        </analyteGroups>
        <formulationAndRoutes>
            <formulationAndRoute>
                <formulationAndRouteId>id0</formulationAndRouteId>
                <formulation>parenteralSolution</formulation>
                <administrationName>Intermittent intravenous infusion</administrationName>
                <administrationRoute>intravenousDrip</administrationRoute>
                <absorptionModel>infusion</absorptionModel>
                <dosages>
